// SPEED ZONE — BREAKNECK — one song: what it plays, how it is arranged, how it sounds.
//
// SPEED ZONE as drum & bass at 174 — THE BANGER. A game alternate of speed, selectable
// from the dev menu (GAME ALTERNATES) and on the desk. Nothing replaces the live song.
// 
// Both of the cabinet's tunes, note for note. THE RIFF (E5 . . B4 . E5 . G5 . E5 . B4 .
// A4 . B4 — what the player hears every lap) screams over a Reese bass playing the
// cabinet's own galloping bass line. THE SYNTH LEAD (speed.js lead4, HORIZON LINES'
// melody: E G B A | G F# E | B D E D | C B A B) is on an electric grand in the build,
// at half speed and re-harmonised (Cmaj7 D Em7 Am B7) in the breakdown, and in drop
// two on a mega-saw and a plain square under the riff (speed.js's own layout) with
// the grand an octave up. Each drop keeps the cabinet's gear changes: eight bars in
// E minor, four in A minor, four in B minor.
// 
//   1–4    intro — the riff on a crystal pluck, strings, sub (the cabinet-screen loop)
//   5–12   build — breakbeat in, the grand on the synth lead; snare roll, riser
//   13–28  DROP — two-step, Reese gallop, screaming riff, pumping saws; E ×8, A ×4, B ×4
//   29–36  breakdown — synth lead at half speed on the grand, Cmaj7 D Em7 Am B7
//   37–40  build — the synth lead's answer phrase, roll, riser
//   41–56  DROP TWO — + the synth lead under the riff (mega-saw, square), grand 8va, ride
//   57–64  outro — riff and grand once more, half-time into the loop (bar 5)
// 
// Stays in E minor at home (the coyote howl and the wink are E minor, baked at the
// song's tempo); the first drop lands 11 s after bar 5.
// 
// 64 bars at 174, 88 s. Written by work/local/_speed-remix-breakneck.mjs through
// work/local/_remix-lib.mjs; re-running it rewrites this file.
//
// SPOT FX — MORE (1 Oct 2026, work/local/_spot-fx-more.mjs): stutter rolls into both drops (12, 40).
//
